{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>To make atonement for him.</b> For when a person eats forbidden fat unintentionally, he brings a sin-offering, and in case of doubt, a guilt-offering for suspension. And sometimes he is certain that he ate forbidden fat, and he brings the offering accordingly, yet he actually ate chelev — and the burnt-offering makes atonement for what he never knows."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:46.337755416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}